    affiliation: "Universidade Federal de Uberlândia, Brazil"
keywords:
  - bioimpedance
  - body composition
  - index validation
  - negative control
  - redundancy
abstract: "BioMS Zaku decomposes indices and predictive equations into vectors of exponents, predicts their redundancy analytically from the log-covariance of the measured variables, and audits each one out of sample against a declared target and a negative control. Demonstrated on bioimpedance."
